- define beneficiary consent;
- define creator and partner splits;
- define unused-credit treatment;
- define monthly reporting;
- do not collect money;
- do not claim charitable or tax status without a qualified review.

For the one-dollar pilot:
- build a real $1 item only if digital fulfillment exists;
- otherwise identify the exact missing dependency;
- do not claim the payment happened;
- preserve Lakisha’s pilot invitation and history record as pending.

For the first public post:
- prepare the still image;
- include the THYLORA math;
- show the help email;
- show the store path;
- route to Chairman review;
- do not publish until the publication gate is satisfied.

For continuity:
- preserve every source phrase;
- record the current phase;
- record the restart point;
- record completed work;
- record blockers;
- record the next action;
- list what the Chairman may be missing.

Return the report in numbered sections. Do not give a compressed summary.
